.TH SPRITEPLOT 1
.SH NAME
spriteplot \- sweep a sprite across the screen
.SH SYNOPSIS
.B temple/spriteplot
.SH DESCRIPTION
.I SpritePlot
is a port of the TempleOS
.B Demo/Graphics/SpritePlot.HC
demonstration.
It runs under
.IR wm (1).
.PP
The "Welcome to TempleOS" banner walks a quarter of the way across the
screen, one pixel every three milliseconds, and then the sprite's size in
bytes is printed.  The original uses this to show that a program drawing
into the persistent device context needs no thirty-times-a-second window
callback: it simply draws and sleeps.
.PP
The controls are:
.TF "any key"
.TP
.B "any key"
Exit, once the sweep has finished
.PD
.SH SOURCE
.B /appl/temple/spriteplot.b
.SH SEE ALSO
.IR temple (1),
.IR spriteedit (1),
.IR wm (1)
